{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/901227-coc-with-totem-spirits","id":901227,"title":"CoC with Totem spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-27T11:58:55-07:00","id":901227,"title":"CoC with Totem spirits","content":"There are rituals presented in the Crone book to allow a witch to deal with spirits on several levels as well as the discipline in the Book of Spirits. Thr BoS gives a reason why mortals cannot form bounds with spirits, the body being unable to the connection, but what about a few kindred from the Circle Crone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T12:11:19-07:00","id":901248,"title":"","content":"You want ot look at the Dead Wolves bloodline, Shadow of Mexico. They deal with totem spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T12:12:04-07:00","id":901249,"title":"","content":"The bad news? There aren't rules regarding the subject, in 1e or 2e.<br /> <br /> The good news? You're free to make them up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T18:29:24-07:00","id":901611,"title":"","content":"Well, vampires can become part of a werewolf pack by connecting with a totem spirit, so I don't see why they wouldn't be able to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T23:38:42-07:00","id":901810,"title":"","content":"Having a Strix as a Coterie totem &quot;spirit&quot; would...n't be the <i>least </i>logical choice. Provided it has (for its kind) motives alien or perverse enough to its kind to make it believable.<br /> <br /> That sounds like a <i>really painful</i> campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:55:34-07:00","id":902196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/901227-coc-with-totem-spirits?p=901249#post901249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bad news? There aren't rules regarding the subject, in 1e or 2e.<br /> <br /> The good news? You're free to make them up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks I wanted to make sure it didn't sound too munchkin or cheesy. They'd be worshipping a Hunger spirit that has be corrupted by addiction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T11:12:20-07:00","id":902821,"title":"","content":"Actually mortals can form totem bonds, even in first edition.<br /> <br /> I don't remember which werewolf book it was in, but it gave rules for such, the fluff being spirits giving out totem benefits to their cults, the result aren't pretty.<br /> <br /> Mortals degenerate, losing attribute dots as their bodies slowly hybridize to mirror their totem.<br /> <br /> It immediately made me think of the Innsmouth look, so I wonder if that was an inspiration, but who knows. <br /> <br /> Since vampire bodies reset with the daysleep, one could certainly argue that they wouldn't suffer from such a fate.<br /> <br /> So a cult of crones gaining totem benefits hardly seems out there, since mortals can do it. <br /> <br /> Another idea one might play with is to adapt the personal totem rules from the Lone Wolves hack from the Werewolf Chronicler's Guide, since it's basically a form of possession, and vampires can be possessed- Personal Totem costs three times as much as normal totem if memory serves, can be improved without upper limit, and represents a totem spirit possessing your body, so you don't have to share the totem benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T05:10:35-07:00","id":903403,"title":"","content":"I think the CoC sort of can get an unofficial totem, those void creatures they can summon with the void cruac style merit. They coukd treat one of those as a totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T07:03:06-07:00","id":903453,"title":"","content":"Mortals benefit from Totem in 2E, so I'm fairly certain the freedom of Toteming has expanded somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T09:30:44-07:00","id":903608,"title":"","content":"Well, in 2e, you can even have packs, complete with totems, without any werewolves in it. In theory, you could have a pack with vampires, mages and changelings, but no wolves, and all bound by a totem. And, of course, supernaturals like vampires can join an existing werewolf pack and contribute totem merit dots as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}